## Documentation — `agent-doc/`

All project documentation lives in `agent-doc/` as one normalised, validated
model — not scattered markdown files. Work with it **only** through the
`docs:*` commands; never hand-edit anything under `agent-doc/docs/`.

Every command runs from the repository root via `--prefix`:

```bash
npm --prefix agent-doc run docs:show                 # the index: everything, priority-ordered
npm --prefix agent-doc run docs:show -- --id k3f     # one document (any unambiguous prefix)
npm --prefix agent-doc run docs:new -- task "…" --area <area>   # file new work
npm --prefix agent-doc run docs:check                # validate; must pass
```

The commands, in the order you meet them:

| | |
|---|---|
| `docs:show` | read — one document assembled in full, or a filtered list (`--type`, `--area`, `--status`, `--on`, `--summary`) |
| `docs:new` | file a document; the ID is minted, never typed — `--on <ID>` links it immediately |
| `docs:set` | change fields on an existing document |
| `docs:link` | relate two documents — one pivot, both directions |
| `docs:rm` | remove a document and everything that hangs off it |
| `docs:check` | validate the whole model; exit 1 on any problem |
| `docs:query` | SQL against a derived index, rebuilt on every run |
| `docs:migrate` | one-time: move a pre-existing database onto `<type>-<suffix>` ids |

Ground rules:

- **`skill-docs-model` is the skill** that explains the whole model — read it
  (`docs:show -- --id skill-docs-model`) before filing anything for the first
  time.
- **Before starting a task**, check `docs:show` for rules, tasks and notes
  linked to the area you are about to touch.
- **IDs are minted by `docs:new`, never typed or guessed.** They look like
  `task-k3f9x2`; any unambiguous prefix resolves, so `k3f` is usually enough.
- **After filing or changing documentation**, run `docs:check` — it must pass.
- `agent-doc/INSTALL.md` is human setup documentation — you do not need it.

